imx8mp-evk: measure the running system with IMA

With the fTPM available from kernel init, turn IMA on for real: the
built-in "tcb" policy measures every executable, mmapped library,
kernel module and root-opened file into the measurement log and PCR 10,
with the ima-ng template and SHA-256. Without a policy IMA records only
boot_aggregate. The options go into mmcargs, which is what the board's
default boot flow (SD, distro boot) uses.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board configuration for the fTPM/IMA setup]

--- a/board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/imx8mp_evk.env
+++ b/board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/imx8mp_evk.env
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
 mmcroot=/dev/mmcblk1p2 rootwait rw
 mmcautodetect=yes
 scriptaddr=0x43500000
-mmcargs=setenv bootargs ${jh_clk} ${mcore_clk} console=${console} root=${mmcroot}
+mmcargs=setenv bootargs ${jh_clk} ${mcore_clk} console=${console} root=${mmcroot} ima_policy=tcb ima_template=ima-ng ima_hash=sha256
 prepare_mcore=setenv mcore_clk clk-imx8mp.mcore_booted
 kernel_addr_r=CONFIG_SYS_LOAD_ADDR
 loadimage=fatload mmc ${mmcdev}:${mmcpart} ${loadaddr} ${image}
